invariant: INV-14
file: srv_ticket.c
catches: srv_test
reason: a ticket whose tag does not verify is decrypted under this server's key
  anyway, so a ticket sealed under another key, or one a client altered,
  opens and hands its bytes to the selection as if this server had sealed
  them. The tag is the only thing that ties a ticket to the key that
  sealed it. test/srv_ticket_tests.h flips one bit at every byte and opens
  under a second key, and requires every one to be refused.

--- old
        0) {
        return CH_EAUTH;
    }
--- new
        0) {
        chacha20_xor(key, nonce, 1, ct, body, sizeof body);
    }
